Business Justification:
I am implementing the Dynamics 365 automated user-provisioning solution. The solution will use an Azure Function with a User-Assigned Managed Identity to detect changes to approved Microsoft Entra ID groups through Microsoft Graph, provision eligible users into Dataverse, activate the appropriate group-team/security-role access before first login, and provide monitoring and failure handling.

The following DEV access is required to build, configure, test, and troubleshoot the solution. Production access is not being requested at this stage.


| #  | Access / Resource Requested                                  | Requested Level                                                                             | Why It Is Needed                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |
| -- | ------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1  | **DEV Azure Subscription / Resource Group**                  | Contributor on the designated DEV resource group                                            | Required to create and configure the Azure Function App, Storage Account, Application Insights, Log Analytics integration, application settings, and related DEV resources.                                                                  |
| 2  | **User-Assigned Managed Identity**                           | Permission to create/configure a DEV UAMI, or have Infrastructure create it                 | The Function will use a managed identity to authenticate to Microsoft Graph and Dataverse without storing client secrets, passwords, or certificates.                                                                                        |
| 3  | **DEV Function App**                                         | Contributor                                                                                 | Required to deploy the .NET isolated Azure Function, configure the managed identity, application settings, timer trigger, and troubleshoot execution.                                                                                        |
| 4  | **DEV Azure Storage Account**                                | Contributor / appropriate Storage data access                                               | Required for Function runtime storage, Graph delta-state persistence, and failed-message/poison-queue handling.                                                                                                                              |
| 5  | **Application Insights / Log Analytics**                     | Contributor or equivalent telemetry-management access                                       | Required to monitor executions, query logs, troubleshoot failures, establish correlation IDs, and configure operational alerts.                                                                                                              |
| 6  | **Microsoft Entra ID – Users and Groups**                    | Directory read access sufficient to inspect the approved DEV groups/users                   | Required to identify and validate the DEV environment security group, role groups, group Object IDs, membership configuration, and users used during provisioning tests.                                                                     |
| 7  | **Microsoft Graph permissions for the DEV Managed Identity** | Approved least-privilege application permissions                                            | Required for the Function to query the approved Entra groups using Microsoft Graph delta queries and retrieve the user attributes necessary for provisioning. Final permission set will be validated using least privilege before approval.  |
| 8  | **DEV Power Platform / Dataverse Environment**               | Environment Admin/System Administrator for development, or equivalent administrator support | Required to validate user provisioning behavior, configure/test application-user access, inspect System Users, Business Units, Entra Group Teams, roles, queues, and troubleshoot Dataverse API operations.                                  |
| 9  | **Dataverse Application User for DEV Managed Identity**      | Permission to create/configure, or Power Platform admin assistance                          | The DEV managed identity must be registered as a Dataverse Application User so the Azure Function can securely call the Dataverse Web API.                                                                                                   |
| 10 | **DEV Dataverse Provisioning Security Role**                 | Permission to create/configure a custom role, or admin assistance                           | Required to create/test the least-privilege integration role needed for user provisioning, System User validation, team/BU operations, and authorized impersonation. System Administrator is not intended for the final production identity. |
| 11 | **Dataverse Web API**                                        | API access through the DEV Application User                                                 | Required to test user synchronization/provisioning, `WhoAmI` impersonation, System User lookup, Business Unit alignment, Group Team/security activation, and ownership readiness.                                                            |
| 12 | **Azure DevOps / Git Repository**                            | Contributor                                                                                 | Required to store the Azure Function source code, manage branches/PRs, maintain version control, and support CI/CD deployment.                                                                                                               |
| 13 | **Azure DevOps Pipeline / Service Connection**               | Ability to build/deploy to DEV, or DevOps-team support                                      | Required to establish repeatable deployments of the Function and related configuration into the DEV environment.                                                                                                                             |
| 14 | **Network / InfoSec Connectivity Approval**                  | Outbound HTTPS (443) from the Function to required Microsoft services                       | Required for the Function to obtain Entra tokens and communicate with Microsoft Graph, DEV Dataverse, Azure Storage, and Azure monitoring services. The proposed design does not require a public inbound webhook.                           |
